Direct scanout at a fractional output scale

Problem: direct scanout never happens on an output with a fractional scale (DP-3
at 1.5). The scanout check compares the surface's integer buffer scale with the
output scale, which can never be equal at 1.5. Every fullscreen game is then
composited. Present since Wayfire 0.9.0.
Fix: remove the scale check and set buffer_dst_box to the full output, so the
display hardware scales a buffer of another size; a driver that cannot fails
the test commit and the frame is composited. Without the box, wlroots would
show such a buffer unscaled in the top-left corner (amdgpu, Intel skl+ accept
that). A viewport crop is refused: some drivers ignore the plane's source
rectangle. Same approach as wlr_scene.
Upstream: https://github.com/WayfireWM/wayfire/issues/3253 (open). The maintainer
agreed on 2026-11-22 to skip the scale check. Reply and PR drafts:
~/Documents/Wayfire direct scanout/; not posted yet.
Remove when: the fix is on main. Check: a fullscreen game at scale 1.5 is
scanned out directly, and a fullscreen client without fractional-scale-v1 fills
the screen.
Base: wayfire 669bbe36.

